.TH tudav n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tudav
.PP
A minimal WebDAV / CardDAV / CalDAV client. Create a client bound to a base URL and credentials, then run PROPFIND / REPORT / GET / PUT / DELETE. Multistatus responses are parsed into resource dicts (href, status, code, etag, contenttype, collection, displayname, and \fBdata\fR for inline calendar/address data).
.PP
Built on the Tcl core \fBhttp\fR package; \fBhttps uses the \fR\fBtls\fR\fB package\fR, loaded lazily on first https request. Basic auth uses \fBtclutils::tubase64\fR; entity text is decoded with \fBtclutils::tuxml\fR. The client does not parse resource bodies — feed a fetched vCard to \fBtclutils::tuvcard\fR or an iCalendar to \fBtclutils::tuical\fR.
.SS API
.CS
set c [::tclutils::tudav::client https://dav.example.com/addressbooks/me/contacts/ \
        -user alice -password secret]
foreach r [::tclutils::tudav::listResources $c] {
    set vcf  [::tclutils::tudav::get $c [dict get $r href]]
    set card [::tclutils::tuvcard::parse $vcf]
    # ...
}
::tclutils::tudav::destroy $c
.CE
.PP
Commands:
.IP \(bu
\fBclient url ?\-user u? ?\-password p? ?\-headers {k v ...}?\fR → client token.
.IP \(bu
\fBpropfind c ?\-path p? ?\-depth 0|1|infinity? ?\-props {...}? ?\-body xml?\fR → list of resource dicts.
.IP \(bu
\fBreport c path xmlBody ?\-depth d?\fR → resource dicts (multiget / calendar\-query).
.IP \(bu
\fBlistResources c ?\-path p?\fR → non\-collection entries \fB{href etag contenttype}\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fBget c path\fR → body (errors on non\-2xx).
.IP \(bu
\fBput c path data ?\-type ct? ?\-etag e?\fR \-> returns the new ETag (if the server reports one); \fBdelete c path ?\-etag e?\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fBlastStatus c\fR → last HTTP status line ; \fBdestroy c\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fBcalendarQuery c path fromIso toIso\fR — CalDAV calendar\-query REPORT for VEVENTs in a time range; each resource dict's \fBdata\fR holds the inline iCal.
.IP \(bu
\fBaddressbookMultiget c path hrefs\fR — CardDAV multiget; \fBdata\fR holds vCards.
.IP \(bu
\fBmkCollection c path ?\-displayname n?\fR — create a plain WebDAV collection.
.IP \(bu
\fBmkAddressbook c path ?\-displayname n?\fR — create a CardDAV address book.
.IP \(bu
\fBmkCalendar c path ?\-displayname n?\fR — create a CalDAV calendar (MKCALENDAR).
.IP \(bu
\fBlistCollections c ?\-path p?\fR — discover child collections under \fBp\fR; dicts \fB{href displayname kind}\fR with \fBkind\fR in addressbook/calendar/collection.
.IP \(bu
\fBcalendarMultiget c path hrefs\fR — CalDAV multiget; \fBdata\fR holds iCalendar.
.IP \(bu
\fBcurrentUserPrincipal c ?\-path p?\fR — DAV:current\-user\-principal href.
.IP \(bu
\fBcalendarHomeSet c principal\fR / \fBaddressbookHomeSet c principal\fR — home hrefs.
.IP \(bu
\fBwellKnown c caldav|carddav\fR — RFC 6764 redirect target, or "".
.IP \(bu
\fBdiscover c ?\-path p?\fR — \fB{principal <href> calendarHome <href> addressbookHome <href>}\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fBgetProperties c ?\-path p? ?\-props {...}?\fR — read collection properties; dict of short\-name \-> value. Known: displayname, calendar\-color, calendar\-description, addressbook\-description, supported\-calendar\-component\-set (a list of comp names).
.IP \(bu
\fBproppatch c path props\fR — set properties (PROPPATCH). \fBprops\fR is a dict of short\-name \-> value (displayname, calendar\-color \fB#rrggbb[aa]\fR, calendar\-description, addressbook\-description). The component set is create\-time only and read\-only here.
.IP \(bu
\fBsyncCollection c path ?\-token t?\fR — RFC 6578 incremental sync. Returns \fB{token <new> changes <resource dicts>}\fR; empty \fB\-token\fR does the initial sync, a returned token feeds the next call. In incremental results a change with \fBcode\fR 404 means the resource was removed.
.PP
Verified end to end against Radicale 3.7 (provision, PUT, REPORT, GET, DELETE) on Tcl 8.6 and 9.x.
.PP
Errors: HTTP failures → \fB{TCLUTILS TUDAV HTTP}\fR; missing tls for https → \fB{TCLUTILS TUDAV TLS}\fR.
